---
title: Vermont Football Officials
description: Rules, mechanics and getting-started information for high school football officials in Vermont — including how to become one.
---

include _includes/mixins/topics.pug

//- The home page is a signpost, not an index.
//-
//- Two audiences arrive here and want different things: people deciding whether
//- to try officiating, and officials already working games. Listing every
//- article and quiz served neither — it put whatever was written most recently
//- on top and made the reader do the sorting. The full lists still live at
//- /information/ and /quizzes/, both one click away in the navbar, so this page
//- curates instead of enumerating.

.text-center.mb-4
  h1.display-6 Vermont Football Officials
  p.lead.mb-2
    | Rules, mechanics and getting-started information for high school football officials in Vermont.
  p.text-secondary.mb-0
    | Varsity football here is worked by crews of five.
    |  Nobody starts out knowing the job — the crew teaches you.

- var count = function(name) { return (collections.information || []).filter(function (item) { return (item.data.tags || []).indexOf(name) !== -1; }).length; }

.row.g-4
  .col-lg-6
    .card
      .card-body.pb-2
        h2.h4.card-title New to officiating
        p.card-text.text-secondary.mb-0
          | You do not need to have played football and you do not need experience officiating anything.
          |  First-year dues are waived.
          |  These four pages, in order, are the whole path from curious to on the field.
      .list-group.list-group-flush
        a.list-group-item.list-group-item-action(href='/information/becoming-an-official/')
          div.fw-semibold Becoming a Football Official
          small.text-secondary What the job is, what it costs, what it pays, and how to start.
        a.list-group-item.list-group-item-action(href='/information/information-for-new-folks/')
          div.fw-semibold Equipment for New Officials
          small.text-secondary What to buy, where to get it, and what to do if the cost is a problem.
        a.list-group-item.list-group-item-action(href='/information/your-first-season/')
          div.fw-semibold Your First Season
          small.text-secondary What to study and in what order, plus what your first game looks like.
        a.list-group-item.list-group-item-action(href='/information/getting-assigned/')
          div.fw-semibold Getting Assigned
          small.text-secondary How games actually reach you — availability, turnbacks and fees.
      //- The recruiting call to action, and the last thing in this column on
      //- purpose: everything above it exists to get someone as far as this button.
      .card-body.pt-3
        a.btn.btn-dark(href='/contact/') Email us about officiating
        p.card-text.small.text-secondary.mt-2.mb-0
          | Most people who do this started by asking one question of one person.

  .col-lg-6
    .card
      .card-body.pb-2
        h2.h4.card-title Already officiating
        p.card-text.text-secondary.mb-0
          | Field reference for officials on a crew: the cards you print and carry, the rules you look up mid-week, and the machinery around the game.
      .list-group.list-group-flush
        a.list-group-item.list-group-item-action(href='/tags/position-cards/')
          div.fw-semibold
            | Position Cards
            if count('Position Cards')
              span.text-secondary.fw-normal.ms-1 (#{count('Position Cards')})
          small.text-secondary Your spot, your keys and your jobs — one card per position on a crew of five.
        a.list-group-item.list-group-item-action(href='/tags/crew-cards/')
          div.fw-semibold
            | Crew Cards
            if count('Crew Cards')
              span.text-secondary.fw-normal.ms-1 (#{count('Crew Cards')})
          small.text-secondary Who has what, one phase of the game at a time, for crews of five and four.
        a.list-group-item.list-group-item-action(href='/information/football-rules-summary/')
          div.fw-semibold Cliff Notes — NFHS Football Rules Book
          small.text-secondary The rule book boiled down, with penalty enforcement in one table.
        a.list-group-item.list-group-item-action(href='/information/clock-officials-cheat-sheet/')
          div.fw-semibold Clock Officials Cheat Sheet
          small.text-secondary For the person on the clock — starts, stops and the untimed down.
        //- Also linked in the New column above. It is the one page both audiences
        //- need — the newcomer to understand how games arrive, the veteran for
        //- turnbacks and playoffs — so it is listed for each, framed for each.
        a.list-group-item.list-group-item-action(href='/information/getting-assigned/')
          div.fw-semibold Getting Assigned
          small.text-secondary Availability, turnbacks, mileage, playoffs and how you get paid.
        a.list-group-item.list-group-item-action(href='/information/foul-weather-procedures/')
          div.fw-semibold Foul Weather Procedures
          small.text-secondary Lightning, delays and when the game stops.
        a.list-group-item.list-group-item-action(href='/quizzes/')
          div.fw-semibold Quizzes
          small.text-secondary Rules questions with a fully cited answer key. Good for a crew meeting.

h2.h6.text-secondary.text-uppercase.mt-5.mb-2 Browse by topic
p.mb-2
  each topic in (topics || [])
    if count(topic.name)
      a.topic-link.badge.rounded-pill.text-bg-light.border.text-decoration-none.me-1(href='/tags/' + topic.slug + '/')= topic.name
